    "narrative": "As we navigate the final stretch of the 2026 season, the optimal approach for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on exploiting high-ceiling matchups where park factors and platoon advantages align. Today, **Mickey Moniak** is our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 75.75 score. He is perfectly positioned to capitalize on a favorable matchup against King, with a significant 14% boost from a premium hitting park and a dynamic platoon advantage. Alongside him, **Isaac Paredes** (69.54) remains a must-start; he is locked into the three-hole and benefits from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.59, making him our highest-projected source of counting stats for the day. While **Brice Turang** carries a solid 54.17 score, his stolen base upside is mitigated slightly by facing a catcher with a quick 1.89s pop time, though his role at the top of the lineup keeps him safely in the active slot.\n\nThe decision-making process for the remaining slots remains cautious due to the scarcity of high-efficiency options in today\u2019s slate. **Moises Ballesteros** (56.02) provides a respectable floor, bolstered by positive wind conditions and a strong spot in the order, narrowly edging out our remaining depth. **Trevor Story** (49.64) rounds out the active roster as a marginal play; while he lacks the elite ceiling of **Mickey Moniak**, his proximity to the 50-point threshold makes him preferable to keeping a bat idle, provided the game caps allow. We are currently managing the availability of **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood**, all of whom are sidelined by team off-days, while **Tyler Soderstrom** remains on the IL, precluding him from consideration. Should any late lineup changes emerge for **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, or **Travis Bazzana**, we will adjust our strategy to prioritize remaining stolen base potential, which remains our primary objective in the final weeks.",
